  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.3.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pyfzf\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/pyfzf/pyfzf-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: dd902e34cffeca9c3082f96131593dd20b4b3a9bba5b9dde1b0688e424b46bd2\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: python -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - setuptools\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    # Not in the upstream metadata, but FzfPrompt() raises SystemError when the\n    # fzf binary is not on PATH, so the wrapper cannot do anything without it.\n    - fzf\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - pyfzf\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n      pip_check: true\n  - script:\n      # Constructing FzfPrompt is what probes PATH for fzf, so this also checks\n      # that the fzf run dependency is actually resolvable.\n      - python -c \"from pyfzf import FzfPrompt; FzfPrompt()\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/nk412/pyfzf\n  summary: Python wrapper for junegunn's fuzzy finder (fzf)\n  description: |\n    pyfzf lets Python code drive fzf, the command-line fuzzy finder. It pipes\n    an iterable of choices to an fzf subprocess and returns the entries the\n    user selected, so a script can offer interactive filtering without\n    implementing its own picker.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  repository: https://github.com/nk412/pyfzf\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
